From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Subject: [PATCH] x86/reboot: quiesce IRQs and stop CPUs before do_kernel_restart()

Commit ae715818c5d7 ("x86/reboot: execute the kernel restart handler upon
machine restart") added do_kernel_restart() to native_machine_restart() so
that drivers registering a restart handler (e.g. a SoC reset controller)
get a chance to reboot the system before falling through to legacy x86
reboot methods.

On platforms whose restart handler reaches its trigger through a single
MMIO write, the bare call is fragile: with IRQs still enabled and other
CPUs running, an interrupt or cross-call can preempt the handler between
the write and the actual reset, the handler returns without effect, and
the system falls through to __machine_emergency_restart(). On hardware
without a working ACPI / KBD / BIOS / EFI reboot path that means a hang.

Wrap the call in a small native_kernel_reboot() helper that pins the
current CPU, halts the others and masks IRQs before invoking
do_kernel_restart(). The helper still forwards @command, so platforms
that act on it (Android-style reboot reasons, vendor recovery modes)
keep working.

Use the same helper from native_machine_emergency_restart() so panic
and sysrq-b also reach the restart handler chain instead of going
straight to legacy methods, with @command set to NULL since the
emergency entry point does not carry one.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
--- a/arch/x86/kernel/reboot.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kernel/reboot.c
@@ -606,6 +606,14 @@ void __attribute__((weak)) mach_reboot_f
 {
 }
 
+static void native_kernel_reboot(char *command)
+{
+	preempt_disable();
+	stop_other_cpus();
+	local_irq_disable();
+	do_kernel_restart(command);
+}
+
 /*
  * To the best of our knowledge Windows compatible x86 hardware expects
  * the following on reboot:
@@ -635,6 +643,8 @@ static void native_machine_emergency_res
 	if (reboot_emergency)
 		emergency_reboot_disable_virtualization();
 
+	native_kernel_reboot(NULL);
+
 	tboot_shutdown(TB_SHUTDOWN_REBOOT);
 
 	/* Tell the BIOS if we want cold or warm reboot */
@@ -779,7 +789,7 @@ static void native_machine_restart(char
 	if (!reboot_force)
 		machine_shutdown();
 
-	do_kernel_restart(command);
+	native_kernel_reboot(command);
 
 	__machine_emergency_restart(0);
 }
